{"title":"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a psychology experiment, an image of a cat or an image of a dog is flashed briefly onto a screen and then Anna is asked to guess whether the image showed a cat or a dog. This process is repeated a large number of times with an equal number of images of cats and images of dogs shown. If Anna is correct 95% of the time when she guesses “dog\" and 90% of the time when she guesses “cat\", determine the ratio of the number of times she guessed “dog\" to the number of times she guessed “cat\".\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of times that Anna guessed cat and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of times that she guessed dog. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870303feff6f491471061a7402eba3e326ba84f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of her guesses for cats were correct and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65a767ee7c06c8ff24f9437751f8d906bdb4854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$95\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of her guesses for dogs were correct, she must have had <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e1253ae5576fe6704bd2fd4fbce29df6756e9d88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.9c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> correct guesses for \"cat\" and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/e/0fe7bb11f0729a1ba01e010041f4ada1e6dce063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.95d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> correct guesses for \"dog,\" meaning that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c5811a909858e5f2e5328e4fd0513cb8ba3ef8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c - 0.9c = 0.1c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" /> of her guesses for \"cats\" were actually on images of dogs and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532d8f5bf6d58f8d930b4a598576bb18e3d479da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d - 0.95d = 0.05d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" /> of her guesses for \"dogs\" were actually on images of cats.\n</p><p>Thus, the number of images of cats that Anna is shown is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab804dee81b187665cbecc4d635f7e743ff1c8e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.9c + 0.05d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" /> and the number of images of dogs that she is shown is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/2/e02330b99a9ef8d5076e5f5ced54d3d6498e9855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.1c + 0.95d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />. These are equal to each other, as given in the problem, so:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/2/e62ac1051e61e85cff3583bbf9c21edece8f5ddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.9c + 0.05d = 0.1c + 0.95d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"216\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5608c447f55d0834cd8e3b42217c4ec8eb79db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.9c - 0.1c = 0.95d - 0.05d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"216\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd17e6eaab696c4a180ee6b0b3a9d8d2402a8b7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.8c = 0.9d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"90\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/b/1bbee7769a9c5e03e9b493b0f8a0b6ed9d563525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{d}{c} = \\frac{0.8}{0.9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"39\" />, so the ratio of the number of times she guessed \"dog\" to the number of times she guessed \"cat\" is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/e/b8ee770238e59bae76861fa330ace13b7a39981b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{8:9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"46\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC\" title=\"2015 CSMC\">2015 CSMC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_1\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 1\">Part A 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_2\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 2\">Part A 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part A 3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_4\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 4\">Part A 4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Part A 5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_A_Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part A Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Part A 6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 1 (page does not exist)\">Part B 1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 2 (page does not exist)\">Part B 2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_CSMC_Problems/Part_B_Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2015 CSMC Problems/Part B Problem 3 (page does not exist)\">Part B 3</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=CEMC_Senior_Competition\" title=\"CEMC Senior Competition\">CEMC Senior Competition</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060758\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 105/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1283/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 134/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2735/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.264      1 Template:CEMC_CIMC/CSMC_box\n100.00%    7.264      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37304:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060758 and revision id 287974. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}